### BUSINESS REPORT:
Crypto Market Analysis Project — Business Summary
1. Business Objective:-
The goal of this project was to analyze cryptocurrency price movements and present reliable, interpretable insights using industry-standard analytics tools, while ensuring consistency and correctness across the reporting pipeline.
2. Design Philosophy:-
Business logic defined once and reused everywhere.
Visualization tools treated as consumers, not calculators.
Clarity, accuracy, and stability prioritized over visual novelty.
3. Data Flow & Governance:=
Raw price data stored centrally in a database.
All calculations standardized in a single analytical layer.
Excel and dashboards consume the same validated metrics, eliminating discrepancies.
Business benefit:
Single source of truth and reduced risk of conflicting numbers.
4. Dashboard Strategy:-
Focused KPIs highlighting price movement behavior.
Simple trend and comparison visuals.
Filters designed to preserve data correctness rather than force advanced UI interactions.
Outcome:
Dashboard is easy to interpret, reliable, and suitable for decision discussions.
5. Business Challenges & Decisions:-
5.1 Tool Stability Risks
BI tool instability caused loss of dashboard components.
Decision: rebuild using simpler, more stable layouts.
Business impact:
Reduced risk of report failure during reviews or demos.
5.2 Feature Trade-offs
Advanced navigation and automation features were evaluated.
But Dropped due to:
1)-Limited business value
2)-Increased maintenance risk
3)-Dependency on paid or cloud services
Business impact:
Lean, maintainable dashboard aligned with real analyst workflows.
5.3 Data Integrity vs Visual Complexity
Continuous time slicers were avoided due to timestamp inconsistencies.
Chose categorical filtering to preserve data meaning.
Business impact:
Prevented misleading trends and incorrect interpretations.
6. Key Business Learnings:-
Reliable analytics matter more than feature-rich dashboards.
Stable, interpretable reports are preferred over complex UI interactions.
Understanding tool limitations is critical for realistic project delivery.
Knowing when to stop adding features is a core analytics skill.
End-to-end ownership ensures accountability and trust in outputs.
7. Business Value Delivered:-
A clean, decision-ready analytics dashboard.
Consistent metrics across tools
